Following yesterday's demonstrations in Paris, where violent clashes erupted between police and protesters, our reporter Antonia Kerrigan returns to place de la République.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2184975a-cae6-11f1-8154-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-130127-131615-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2184975a-cae6-11f1-8154-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-130127-131615-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">265d43d0-cae6-11f1-a4a9-b7e4c9b2dcc0</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:51:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Atlanta’s iconic tavern marks Georgia’s past with an eye on future as midterms approach</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-atlanta-iconic-tavern-marks-georgia-past-eye-future-midterms-approach-ossoff-collins</link><description>
Since it was established in 1956, Manuel’s Tavern in Atlanta has hosted legendary Democratic leaders while its founder played a key role in the city’s move from a Republican to Democratic stronghold. With the state’s Democratic Senator Jon Ossoff leading the polls in the midterms amid rumours of a future presidential run, the tavern is once more at the heart of the political action.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa2b4854-c967-11f1-a45e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/manuels-main.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa2b4854-c967-11f1-a45e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/manuels-main.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">08f298ba-c968-11f1-84d4-7b0775633891</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:15:04 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fa2b4854-c967-11f1-a45e-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/manuels-main.jpg">© Branden Camp, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Out-of-control truck kills 13 at Hindu festival in India</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-out-of-control-truck-kills-13-at-hindu-festival-in-india</link><description>
A speeding truck in India killed 13 people when it ploughed into a crowd at a Hindu festival, officials said on Sunday, with President Droupadi Murmu describing the deaths as "heartbreaking".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eab05edc-cae3-11f1-bd72-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-121827-121952-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/eab05edc-cae3-11f1-bd72-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-121827-121952-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ef82c0a8-cae3-11f1-bb9a-01e0b5eaecde</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:14:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Riots in Tirana enter a fifth day as Albania's anti-government protests escalate</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-riots-in-tirana-enter-a-fifth-day-as-albania-s-anti-government-protests-escalate</link><description>
Clashes broke out near the Albanian prime minister’s office in the capital, Tirana, on Saturday as anti-government riots entered a fifth day.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62af44a8-cae3-11f1-9366-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-111149-111349-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/62af44a8-cae3-11f1-9366-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-111149-111349-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">678afb98-cae3-11f1-86ab-cb0ddd5ab1e1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:06:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Protests "brought the entire population together for a common purpose"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-protests-brought-the-entire-population-together-for-a-common-purpose</link><description>
This weekend, in cities across France, some 800,000 protesters, including students, railway workers and members of the Yellow Vest movement, took to the streets in largely peaceful nationwide demonstrations. Sparked by a month of high school student protests over educational inequality and crumbling school facilities, the movement has grown into a broader outcry over the cost of living, public spending and climate inaction, as people across France say they have reached their breaking point.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b3222c4-cad2-11f1-9b89-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-101748-102037-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b3222c4-cad2-11f1-9b89-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-101748-102037-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5fffff24-cad2-11f1-a1a3-2f27257a22bd</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:05:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Who took part in Saturday's protests?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-who-took-part-in-saturday-s-protests</link><description>
Weeks of student protests over poor conditions in schools and rising anger over the cost of living fuelled calls for a nationwide demonstration on October 17, bringing together youth activists and supporters of the Yellow Vest movement.
 
The main grievance was the cost of living. The protesters demonstrating against it 'didn't get what they wanted', analyses France 24's Shirli Sitbon.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b40d3708-cad2-11f1-906d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-823ce114.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b40d3708-cad2-11f1-906d-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-823ce114.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">df14a860-cad1-11f1-bbaa-0bdd7c1dbb15</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:03:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France: Who was behind the violence at Saturday's protests?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-who-was-behind-the-violence-at-saturday-s-protests</link><description>
Violent clashes, fires, vandalism and looting marred demonstrations across France on Saturday as hundreds of thousands of people marched against the rising cost of living and poor conditions in schools. The French Interior Ministry said about 400 people were arrested nationwide. Our partner TV station France 2 examined who was involved in the violence during Saturday's protests.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1ff195a-cad0-11f1-b9ce-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-101142-101423-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c1ff195a-cad0-11f1-b9ce-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-101142-101423-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c6d470a6-cad0-11f1-82c8-85d457665d2b</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:01:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>France protests: Did the government make the wrong decisions?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261018-france-protests-did-the-government-make-the-wrong-decisions</link><description>
Police in Paris said Sunday they had arrested a "record" 855 people over protest-related violence in the capital the day before, with the prosecutor's office saying more than 500 were being held in custody. France 24's Shirli Sitbon analyses.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6223078a-cad0-11f1-8c01-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-100442-101117-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6223078a-cad0-11f1-8c01-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261018-100442-101117-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">67015810-cad0-11f1-a23d-eb1e66ddfb75</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:00:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>PSG back on top of Ligue 1 after stunning Strasbourg comeback</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261018-ligue-1-psg-back-on-top-of-ligue-1-after-stunning-strasbourg-comeback</link><description>
After trailing Strasbourg for more than 60 minutes, the Parisians called upon their substitutes to turn the game around. Following their spectacular Champions League victory over Manchester City and ahead of their clash with FC Barcelona, PSG are brimming with confidence.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f6628de-ca98-11f1-8a9c-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3LB6RQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f6628de-ca98-11f1-8a9c-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3LB6RQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">66c8f1ba-ca98-11f1-ab75-334b688eb6eb</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:48:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 A demonstrator died from 'cardiorespiratory arrest' during Paris protests, police say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">d84b56ee-cac9-11f1-acc0-c37be56a77f8</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:06:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Months-long Indonesia wildfires spew toxic haze across Southeast Asia</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-months-long-indonesia-wildfires-spew-toxic-haze-across-southeast-asia</link><description>
Parts of southern Southeast Asia have been put under the highest-level haze alert as wildfires that have swept Indonesia for months continue to belch toxic smoke across the region. The seasonal wildfires are worse this year due to the drought conditions caused by a severe "super-El Nino" effect.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/959c6e42-cab9-11f1-bcc1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T172531Z-1337943422-RC29QNASKLJ4-RTRMADP-3-ASIA-WEATHER-INDONESIA-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/959c6e42-cab9-11f1-bcc1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T172531Z-1337943422-RC29QNASKLJ4-RTRMADP-3-ASIA-WEATHER-INDONESIA-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e45050c0-caba-11f1-85b5-bd1110e119fe</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 06:30:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/959c6e42-cab9-11f1-bcc1-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T172531Z-1337943422-RC29QNASKLJ4-RTRMADP-3-ASIA-WEATHER-INDONESIA-WILDFIRE.jpg">© Abriansyah Liberto, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>India's 'cockroach' movement founder released from police custody</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261018-india-s-cockroach-movement-founder-released-from-police-custody</link><description>
Indian police released Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke from detention on Saturday after the activist was detained ahead of a rally calling for the resignation of India's chief election commissioner. Two other CJP leaders remain in custody after having been arrested while demonstrating at a protest site that police had ruled off-limits.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8ff30cc-cab4-11f1-8c54-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KJ7R8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8ff30cc-cab4-11f1-8c54-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KJ7R8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6df91d22-cab4-11f1-9715-9b17793e8591</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:47:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b8ff30cc-cab4-11f1-8c54-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3KJ7R8.jpg">© Arun Sankar, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Around 1,500 shops and retailers damaged during French protests, trade group says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france</link><description>
Roughly 1,500 shops and retailers were damaged during the demonstrations that swept France on the weekend, many of them looted, the head of the Retail and Trade Federation said Sunday. Interior Minister Laurent Nuñez said that police had arrested more than 1,800 people as outbursts of arson and looting broke out on the margins of peaceful marches. Follow out liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9aecc2c-cadc-11f1-93d3-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T095418Z-932457184-RC2J5OAZZ1QE-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9aecc2c-cadc-11f1-93d3-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T095418Z-932457184-RC2J5OAZZ1QE-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">537a7882-caa1-11f1-a119-73fa622837ec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:09:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a9aecc2c-cadc-11f1-93d3-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T095418Z-932457184-RC2J5OAZZ1QE-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg">© Benoit Tessier, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Rubio says Trump to 'analyze' global impact of Russia sanctions during pause</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-rubio-says-trump-russia-sanctions-waiver-designed-to-analyze-global-impact</link><description>
US Secretary of State Marco Rubio said Saturday that US President Donald Trump’s decision to waive sanctions and tariffs on Russia would last 60 days, as the move drew bipartisan criticism and raised fears in Ukraine that Washington could ease further restrictions on Moscow.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">25029a10-ca9d-11f1-aa47-9186c059e688</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 02:39:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1b46d8a0-c7e7-11f1-819e-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/dcd8c89867be21a42771dcc4bb966f7a0278e690.jpg">© Mark Schiefelbein, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>‘Standing up for democracy’: Atlanta ‘No Kings’ rally draws Trump critics ahead of midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261018-standing-up-for-democracy-atlanta-no-kings-rally-draws-trump-critics-ahead-of-us-midterms</link><description>
“No Kings, Vote Now” was the theme of a rally in Atlanta, one of many organised across the US on Saturday. While many demonstrators denounced US President Donald Trump’s policies, organisers said the rally was aimed at getting out the vote in the November 3 midterm elections and protecting democracy in America.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">174d7436-ca8d-11f1-b7da-d91d395a4215</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:50:29 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f5ef54b2-ca8c-11f1-b97e-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26290606906702.jpg">© Jose Luis Magana, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Looters seize on massive French protests to raid and vandalise shops</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-looters-seize-massive-french-protests-raid-vandalise-shops-france</link><description>
Looters on Saturday seized the opportunity to raid and vandalise a host of shops and businesses across France – from bakeries and supermarkets to tech stores – as hundreds of thousands of people took to the streets to protest higher living costs and other grievances.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fab94d12-ca51-11f1-a0cb-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/cc2ac62c67a25e9ff25aff593865d3fa117e6424.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fab94d12-ca51-11f1-a0cb-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/cc2ac62c67a25e9ff25aff593865d3fa117e6424.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad1aa604-ca66-11f1-bf9f-4962be607a4d</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 20:15:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fab94d12-ca51-11f1-a0cb-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/cc2ac62c67a25e9ff25aff593865d3fa117e6424.jpg">© Jeff Pachoud, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><title>🔴 Live: Chaotic scenes as organisers of French protests claim 800,000 have taken to streets</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261017-live-france-s-yellow-vests-throw-their-weight-behind-mounting-student-protests</link><description></description><guid isPermaLink="false">c96c031a-ca4e-11f1-b486-d7972d288408</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:18:35 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>India: Police crack down on New Delhi protests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-india-police-crack-down-on-new-delhi-protests</link><description>
Student activist Neha Bora, a prominent face of the protests, ‌who was detained on Friday as she tried to reach central Delhi with dozens of supporters, was released on Saturday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847e0698-ca1e-11f1-a4f6-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261017-121203-121358-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/847e0698-ca1e-11f1-a4f6-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261017-121203-121358-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">898494ae-ca1e-11f1-ad9d-c99dd98fcfb8</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:29:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: Amazon deforestation at 40-year low</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-brazil-amazon-deforestation-at-40-year-low</link><description>
In Brazil, deforestation in the Amazon has reached its lowest level in 40 years. President Lula is bolstering his environmental record just over a week before the second round of the presidential election, in which he faces Flávio Bolsonaro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7770bf44-ca42-11f1-865c-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261017-142458-142642-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7770bf44-ca42-11f1-865c-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261017-142458-142642-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7c5d2402-ca42-11f1-b9c0-2db19636fbe1</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:07:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Ukraine war: "Mothers of Kherson" opera opens in Poland</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-ukraine-war-mothers-of-kherson-opera-opens-in-poland</link><description>
"Mothers of Kherson" has opened at Poland's National Opera. The performance was co-produced with New York's Metropolitan Opera and created in close association with Save Ukraine, a group helping to bring back Ukrainian children who remain in Russia. More than four years after Russia's invasion of Ukraine, the opera aims to "reawaken" global interest in the war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f500ace-ca41-11f1-8347-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261017-170858-171041-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f500ace-ca41-11f1-8347-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261017-170858-171041-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6473984a-ca41-11f1-9a2a-83ffe5fb92ec</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:57:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Protests in France: "Two fires broke out in Place de la République"</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261017-protests-in-france-two-fires-broke-out-in-place-de-la-r%C3%A9publique</link><description>
Police and protesters clashed in Paris and other French cities on Saturday, with smoke from fires and tear gas filling the air at demonstrations nationwide against high prices, ahead of elections to replace President Emmanuel Macron. "Two fires broke out in Place de la République," reports France 24's Antonia Kerrigan from the ground.
